# `GENRE-NODE-SPELLING`: under `statechart`, `node` and `edge` are LINE ERRORS with the named
# diagnostic. This is the asymmetry with `flowchart`, where `node` STAYS legal:
# there a stage can have a role THE SOURCE DOES NOT STATE, and a bare `node` is
# the only spelling for that (`BARE-NODE-MEANING`) — a statechart has one kind of node, so
# nothing is left for `node` to mean and it is simply the old word.
figdown 0.2 statechart
node locked "LOCKED"
state unlocked "UNLOCKED"
edge locked -[coin]-> unlocked
transition unlocked -[push]-> locked
